{"diagnosis": "The incumbent (dev_exact 0.9102) shows exact_by_visit = [0.9297, 0.918, 0.9102]: accuracy strictly degrades with each additional visit, and the adaptive policy already achieves 0.9336 at ~1.10 visits. The extra visits inject recurrent drift rather than signal (relation is unused in this task, so the relation branch of 'relation+mean' contributes noise and FLOPs). Recent history is consistent: visits=2 promoted in deduction (1.0) and hurt elsewhere, verifier_visits=2 helped research (0.7676) but not curation (0.8203), and latent_steps=1 beat the default in kernel_h4 (0.998). The stopping module is small (4 actions, 11 per-candidate features), so deeper recurrent depth is more likely to overfit than to help.",
 "proposals": [
  {"config": {"visits": 2}, "rationale": "Exact_by_visit is monotone decreasing (0.9297/0.918/0.9102), so the 3rd visit costs ~0.008 with no gain. Dropping to 2 visits retains the best-visit accuracy (0.9297) while cutting ~1/3 of recurrent FLOPs (3.34M -> ~2.2M) and params stay at 11683. Predicted gain vs incumbent ~+0.008 to +0.015 on dev_exact.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.925, "falsification": "Measured dev_exact < 0.9102 (or visit-2 exact ≤ 0.918), or by_visit still declines past visit 2."},
  {"config": {"latent_steps": 1}, "rationale": "With only 4 candidates and a 1-step horizon-2 stopping decision, 2 latent steps per cycle add a nonlinear recurrent drift term z<-net(x+y+z) that the data cannot constrain; reducing to 1 step halves the latent-update chain length and should reduce overfitting/drift. Evidence from deduction family: latent_steps=1 gave 0.998 vs 1.0 baseline at kernel_h4. Predicted +0.005 to +0.015.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.925, "falsification": "Measured dev_exact < 0.9102, or exact_by_visit no longer improves at visit 1 (i.e., latent depth was actually load-bearing)."},
  {"config": {"verifier_visits": 2}, "rationale": "The stopping task explicitly selects 'verify' as an action, so the host feedback channel (verified, ok, diag0, diag1) is the main signal for calibrating the verify-vs-stop tradeoff. The incumbent uses only 1 in-loop verifier call; feeding the structured diagnostics back on a second visit gives the recurrent state one more observation of the verifier outcome, which should raise calibration (ece 0.021) and exact success on verify-heavy roots. Predicted +0.005 to +0.015 dev_exact.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.925, "falsification": "Measured dev_exact < 0.9102 or ece worsens, indicating the extra verifier feedback injects noise rather than signal (as in curation where verifier_visits=2 gave 0.8203)."}
 ]}
